+**What compaction keeps (the owner's worry, 2026-10-22):** the system prompt, CLAUDE.md and tool definitions sit outside the conversation and are kept verbatim; the conversation, including a role readme or brief injected into the first message, is summarized. ✅ (2026-10-23: the role readme now lives in the system prompt, which survives compaction, plus a short role reminder after each compaction; [context-drift.md](../../../public/framework/ai/doc/context-drift.md).) Originally: so after a compaction node must re-inject the role readme and the brief verbatim (the `SessionStart:compact` hook already re-adds a line for VS Code tabs). Alternative: summarize and start a fresh session with the role readme as its first message.
+
+## The owner, 2026-10-23: compact before sleep
+
+✅ **Built (`Agent.sleep_compact()` in `Servex/agents/Agents.js`):** going dormant used to never compact. Now an
+agent about to sleep with more than 100k tokens (or half the window, whichever is lower; per role as
+`compact_after.sleep`) runs `/compact` first, then sleeps, so it wakes small. It runs at the sleep moment, which is
